From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grigory Evko <grigory@evko.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:41:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] c++: add -fannotations-on-definition-only

An annotation on a declaration of a class or enumeration that is not its
definition can count as an annotation of the type: a forward declaration
before the definition, an opaque enumeration declaration before the
definition, a declaration of a class template before or after its
definition, a declaration of a partial specialization after its
definition, an explicit instantiation, and the declaration of a nested
class or of a member class template in its class.  Such a declaration
changes what std::meta::annotations_of gives for the type, but only in
the translation units that contain it.  Two units can then see different
annotations of the same type, and a unit can give a type an annotation
that its definition does not have.

The new option -fannotations-on-definition-only makes an annotation on
each declaration of a class or enumeration that is not its definition an
error, before and after the definition: an elaborated-type-specifier
(also in a friend declaration, a typedef, a parameter or a template
argument), an opaque-enum-specifier, and an attribute before or after the
decl-specifiers of a declaration with no declarator.  The diagnostic is
an error, so no diagnostic pragma can turn it off, and -fpermissive does
not change it.

With the option, the definition of an enumeration after an opaque
declaration also carries its annotations.  Without the option,
decl_attributes ignores each type attribute of that definition with
-Wattributes, because the opaque declaration completed the type.  An
opaque declaration in one unit then removes the annotations of the type
in that unit.

Without the option the compiler behaves as before.  The option does not
change an annotation on a function, a variable, a data member, a
parameter, a namespace or a type alias.

gcc/c-family/ChangeLog:

	* c.opt (fannotations-on-definition-only): New option.

gcc/cp/ChangeLog:

	* cp-tree.h (diagnose_annotation_on_declaration): Declare.
	* decl.cc (diagnose_annotation_on_declaration): New function.
	(check_tag_decl): Refuse an annotation of a declaration with no
	declarator that does not define its type.
	(attach_definition_annotations): New function.
	(start_enum): Use it for the definition of an enumeration that an
	opaque declaration completed.
	* parser.cc (cp_parser_elaborated_type_specifier): Refuse an
	annotation.
	(cp_parser_enum_specifier): Refuse an annotation of an
	opaque-enum-specifier.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* doc/invoke.texi (C++ Dialect Options): Document
	-fannotations-on-definition-only.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* g++.dg/reflect/annotation_definition1.C: New test.
	* g++.dg/reflect/annotation_definition2.C: New test.
	* g++.dg/reflect/annotation_definition3.C: New test.
	* g++.dg/reflect/annotation_definition4.C: New test.
	* g++.dg/reflect/annotation_definition5.C: New test.
